WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.901
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.336
is an Emmy- and
Tony Award-winning actor

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.104
you know from movies like
"The Birdcage"

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.907
and "The Lion King," as well as
shows like "The Gilded Age"

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.943
and "Only Murders
in the Building."

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.811
He's currently starring
in "Pictures from Home"

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.145
on Broadway's Studio 54.

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:14.780
And you can see him
in "Beau Is Afraid,"

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.615
which is in theaters now.
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.785
-What is the room is?

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:21.187
-This is a room in our house,

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.090
but it's your home
for as long as you need.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.325
My name's Grace.
[ Knock on door ]

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:29.295
Oh, this is Roger.
This is my husband.

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:36.803
-Hey, guy.
Welcome back.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.838
Thought you'd sleep in, huh?

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.373
-Roger's a very
respected surgeon.

00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:44.410
He's the one who dressed
and treated your wounds.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.378
-You're a lucky man.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.948
[ Device beeps ]

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.351
-What is --
what is this?

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.619
-That's my little
assistant health monitor.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.621
Keeps track of your condition.

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:56.923
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.692
our good friend Nathan Lane,
everybody!

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.527
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:21.547 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:24.116
Look at you!
Look at how fit you are!

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:26.785
-Oh, jogging over here,
I saw Tucker Carlson

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:29.522
in a bar chugging Bud Light.
He's upset.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.723
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, no!

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.858
-He is so upset.
-He is upset.

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:33.993
-Oh, Seth, I --

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.094
-It breaks your heart,
doesn't it?

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.430
-Yeah. Eeee!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.199
You know, I see you backstage.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:43.435
-I thought we were doing
a podcast, but then it hit me.

00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:46.673
This is just your "Every day
is Casual Friday" look.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.141
-Yeah.
-And I have to --

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:51.077
I have to admit
that it has inspired me.

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:54.414
I mean, look at you. You --
You are a rhapsody in J.Crew.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.415
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:59.319
I love that you brought
normcore fashion to late night,

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:02.688
and with this look,
you have totally embraced

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:05.758
the role
of America's late-night zaddy!

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.226
-Oh, well, thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:09.561
Thank you so much.

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:11.363
-You know, I --

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:13.700
I used to dress
like I was interviewing

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.468
with the C.E.O.
of a tech start-up,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:19.004
but then you, you --
you showed me the way.

00:02:19.004 --> 00:02:21.640
You showed me that I was
just trying too hard

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.111
and it was time
to finally give up

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:28.948
and embrace the joy
of the tracksuit.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.517
-Yeah.
-I love tracksuits.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.452
-It's lovely.
-Tracksuit.

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:35.154
It's fashion's way of saying,

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.223
"I have no more [bleep]
to give."

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.759
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.996
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:46.365
Right? You know,
now I can look athletic

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:49.302
and I don't have
to do a damn thing.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:52.238
I always look like
I'm about to go for a run,

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.173
but something
more important came up.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.507
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.507 --> 00:02:56.542
You know, the last time --

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.011
I was supposed to be here
a while ago.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.645
-Yeah, but I had COVID.
We had to --

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:01.581
-Now, do you believe
it's real?

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:04.350
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:08.955
And the time --
the time before that,

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.255
it was the height
of the pandemic.

00:03:10.255 --> 00:03:11.290
There was no audience.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.025
It was like sailing
on a ghost ship,

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.160
just me desperately
trying to make you

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.428
and three cameramen laugh.

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:18.764
-Yeah.
-So -- But here we are.

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.733
-And here we are with a really,
really nice audience.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.501
-Really nice.
-It's pretty nice.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.803
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:28.674
-We are -- We are --
We're reunited showbiz brothers

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:31.376
like Woody Harrelson
and Matthew McConaughey,

00:03:31.376 --> 00:03:34.780
the greatest "Maury Povich"
episode that never was.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.248
[ Laughter ]
Yes.

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:40.052
-You -- I want to compliment you
on something, which is,

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:43.556
since the last time I saw you,
you won an Emmy, sir,

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.859
for your work in "Only..."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.696
The wonderful show
"Only Murders in the Building,"

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:51.730
which just a tremendous cast

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.166
and one of the best things
in the world,

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.068
which is a television show
that got made in New York City.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.537
-I know. And with Marty Short
and Steve Martin

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.238
and Selena Gomez.
-Yeah, that's a --

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:02.040
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.211
-Yes, it was --
It was my seventh nomination.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.712
It was nice to finally win,

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:09.381
although it was
a silent episode.

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:12.185
So all these years, the Academy

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:14.153
was just waiting for me
to shut up.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.554
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:18.557
-You -- This is
the final week of a show.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.092
-That's right.
-You've done a lot of --

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:22.228
-Beautiful play.
-And you've done many

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.396
over the years.
How are you with endings?

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.532
Do you get a little bittersweet

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.267
when you wrap up
a show like this?

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:31.370
-Well, this one in particular.
I have loved doing this play.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.072
It's a beautiful play
by Sharr White,

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.408
directed by Bart Sher,
and starring the wonderful

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.844
Danny Burstein
and Zoe Wanamaker.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.412
And this is --
Yes, this is our last week.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:42.715
So if you're in town,
come to Studio 54 Theatre.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.684
And, really, because
I've been thinking,

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:47.085
this is probably
my theatrical swan song,

00:04:47.085 --> 00:04:48.387
my last Broadway show.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.489
-Now, that -- that is very --
[ Audience booing ]

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:51.623
That's problematic.

00:04:51.623 --> 00:04:53.625
-Well, you see, Seth,

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.761
things have gotten crazy
on the Broadway now.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:57.430
I'm sure you've read about it.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.931
Audiences are out of control.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.266
People are pooping
in the audience.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.767
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.302
-They're heckling the actors.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:07.206
There's fistfights, dog fights,
deliveries from DoorDash.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.509
-No! Mid-show.
DoorDash will show up mid-show?

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:13.145
-Beer pong.
People are having sex,

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:14.780
not even waiting
until intermission.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.916
It's a nightmare.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.118
-That's very hard.
As an actor, that's very hard.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.686
-Well, the pooping is the worst.
-Yeah.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:21.987
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.987 --> 00:05:25.324
And because it's happening
with alarming frequency

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:28.260
on any given night
in a Broadway theater,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.463
the 11:00 number is two.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:33.399
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:36.001
No, if you're gonna --
if you're gonna crap

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:39.005
in the aisle, save it
for a Southwest flight.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.640
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.610
Anyway, I was reminded
of our conversation,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.179
and I think I may have
one more show.

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:49.515
-I'm so glad you said that,
because we have talked about --

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.951
You know, we have
this collaboration in the works.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.786
-"Cicada, Cicada."
-"Cicada, Cicada."

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.188
-Just say it.
-Just say it.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.422
-I mean, the audience
wants to hear.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:06:00.326
"Cicada, Cicada" is a show.
And we might --

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:02.695
We might be closer
to getting it on its feet.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:05.465
Do you want to remind people
of the plot as you remember it?

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.266
-Sure. Yes.
The basic plot line is,

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.901
our dear friend,
Christine Baranski,

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.903
would play a cicada
who comes to New York,

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:13.472
not realizing
she only has 17 days,

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:18.010
the life span of a cicada,
to live her best Big Apple life.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:22.014
She's befriended by a very
gregarious cockroach,

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.350
played by the great
Harvey Fierstein,

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.751
in Times Square.

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:29.455
And he actually resides
in the glamorous apartment

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.357
of a big Broadway star,
played by me.

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:33.893
-There you go.
-And I've come to terms

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:36.228
with the fact
that this is a version of me

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:38.297
with a cockroach-infested
apartment.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.865
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:43.369
I don't -- I don't like it,
but I've come to terms with it.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:46.104
And a lot of the New York Mets

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:47.639
will be playing
supporting roles.

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:50.376
-Yeah.
-Now, I think first baseman

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:54.046
Pete Alonso would be an inspired
choice for the antagonist.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.015
-Yeah.
-Perhaps the exterminator.

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.450
-Oh, very good.
-And we have the tagline,

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.120
"Cicada, Cicada" --
The whole town is abuzz.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.554
So...
-There you go.

00:07:02.554 --> 00:07:04.490
-...aside from not having
a script,

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.159
I think we're 90% there.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:09.895
Now, the big news is
that I reached out

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.697
to two of my oldest
and dearest friends,

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.032
Marc Shaiman
and Scott Wittman,

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:15.367
the Tony-winning geniuses
behind "Hairspray"...

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:17.136
-Geniuses.
-And their current smash hit

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.871
"Some Like It Hot,"
and I asked them

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:22.074
if they would write the score,
and they said, yes, they're in!

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.609
-So...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:27.113
-So...
[ Laughs ]

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.414
So the next time I'm here --

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.248
I have another movie
coming out this summer.

00:07:30.248 --> 00:07:34.887
The next time I'm here,
so it'll be very soon,

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:37.056
it will be --
if we work out the billing

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:41.027
and all the deals go through,
it'll be me, Christine Baranski,

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:42.928
Harvey Fierstein,
and the New York Mets

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:47.199
in the act-one finale of
"Cicada, Cicada."

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:50.169
What I'm saying is,
start sewing the costumes now.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:53.306
-I am so excited.
Your enthusiasm for this is --

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:55.107
It's incredible to me.
-I can't wait.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.509
-You mentioned you have a movie
coming out this summer.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:58.477
You have this --
You know, we showed a clip

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:01.547
of this movie, Joaquin Phoenix,
the great Amy Ryan, another

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:03.882
"Only Murders in the Building"
alum right there.

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:05.284
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:09.255
-And this director has done
some of the trippiest movies

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:11.123
in recent years.
He did "Midsommar."

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:13.125
He did the fantastic film
"Hereditary."

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.927
-Yes.
This is his third film.

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:17.529
-This is his third film.
This is very cool.

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:21.366
And, I mean, a sort of
out-there plot, would you say?

00:08:21.366 --> 00:08:23.502
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:24.970
I would say it's --

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.606
You know, look, it's --

00:08:27.606 --> 00:08:29.174
I'll be honest, it's --

00:08:29.174 --> 00:08:31.009
I think it's
an extraordinary film.

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:35.715
And I think he's -- he's
an astonishing young director.

00:08:35.715 --> 00:08:38.083
But it's been
a divisive film.

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:39.918
You know, it's --

00:08:39.918 --> 00:08:41.354
There's been a lot of chatter

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:43.489
about the fact
that it's three hours.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:46.392
And as I like to say,
it's not a prostate exam.

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:47.959
It's --
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.959 --> 00:08:50.763
It's the --
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:52.731
You know, it's a unique

00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:55.867
and challenging
cinematic experience.

00:08:55.867 --> 00:08:58.637
And for those who want that,
there it is.

00:08:58.637 --> 00:09:00.172
-And there's less
of that every year.

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.207
-Oh, I know.
-So I embrace that.

00:09:02.207 --> 00:09:04.577
-Because I mean, you know,
a $15 ticket

00:09:04.577 --> 00:09:07.780
to see Joaquin Phoenix emote for
80 minutes would be a bargain.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.449
To see him do it for 100 minutes
would be an even better deal.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:13.219
But what if I told you, Seth,
you got Joaquin Phoenix,

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:14.987
the greatest actor
of his generation,

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:17.256
for 80 minutes
and then 100 more minutes

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.791
for the same low price?
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:20.259
-That's fantastic.

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:23.729
-And at no additional charge,
you get Amy Ryan,

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.831
yours truly,
Parker Posey, Patti LuPone,

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.632
and I'll even throw in
Richard Kind.

00:09:27.632 --> 00:09:30.135
-Richard Kind?!
-Richard Kind!

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:31.570
And a Perfect Pasta Pot.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.773
You'd probably say
it's too good to be true.

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:36.809
And you'd be right.
There's no Pasta Pot...

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:38.177
[ Laughter ]

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:41.012
...but there is Richard Kind.
-Richard Kind.

00:09:41.012 --> 00:09:42.781
-And so
it's a pretty sweet deal.

00:09:42.781 --> 00:09:44.516
What are you people
waiting for?!

00:09:44.516 --> 00:09:46.651
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:09:46.651 --> 00:09:50.956
-One more time for my friend
Nathan Lane, everybody!

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:53.726
"Pictures from Home"
is on Broadway at Studio 54.

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:55.528
"Beau is Afraid"
is in theaters now.

00:09:55.528 --> 00:09:57.763
We'll be right back
with Congresswoman Katie Porter.

